I look at a counter nearby.
There is a large glass jar there.
There are sweet baked goods in the glass jar.
I want something sweet.
I see the waiter.
I call him.
"Bhaiya, please listen," I say.
He comes near my table.
"Yes madam, please speak," he says.
I point to the glass jar.
"Is fresh mawa cake available?" I ask.
"Yes, it is available here," the waiter says.
"Please give me one slice of mawa cake," I say.
"Okay, I will bring it," he says.
"Thank you," I say.
I happily wait for the sweet treat.
